cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite the associated paper:
  "Singularity: The Illusion of Dynamic Security".
title: "TASCP / Singularity Reproducibility Artifact: Empirical Autopsy of Stateful Moving-Target Defenses for DNN-based NIDS"
abstract: >-
  Artifact for the paper "Singularity: The Illusion of Dynamic Security",
  evaluating whether a momentum-conditioned Givens rotation of the constraint
  manifold (TASCP) can prevent iterative white-box adversaries from crafting
  adversarial examples against deep network intrusion detectors. The artifact
  contains the defense and attack implementations, machine-checked Lean 4 formal
  proofs, trained checkpoints, dataset preprocessing, archived result records,
  and verification tooling to reproduce every table and figure of the paper.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
    affiliation: "Redacted for double-blind review"
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
keywords:
  - adversarial machine learning
  - network intrusion detection
  - stateful defenses
  - gradient masking
  - moving target defense
  - formal verification
  - lean 4
